Funding-Text = {This work was supported by the International Initiative for Impact
   Evaluation (3ie) {[}TW14.1006]. The funder has influenced the use of a
   common outcome measure for latrine use as well as other variables like
   functionality and use to enable comparability with other ongoing trials.
   Specifically, before the trial was initiated, the funder organized all
   teams that received funding to discuss and agree upon how the outcome
   (latrine use) should be measured. This involved a series of email
   exchanges to first communicate the importance of a common outcome
   measure and get all teams to agree to use a common measure. The funder
   (3ie), along with the Research Institute for Compassionate Economics
   (r.i.c.e.), then worked with all teams via email by proposing a common
   measure and then iteratively adapting the measure based on feedback by
   our team and all other teams involved. Finally, 3ie held a workshop in
